        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=TopicQuote&TOPIC_ID=1141&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=Dear+Verant+%28reposted%29"><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Dear Verant,</P><P>Good luck with your continued success.  With your attitudes toward customer service I expect soon, you will not have as many issues with overcrowded servers and zones.  </P><P>I promised my self the very first time I died to a “verified bug” and your GM support staff would not do anything about it that if it happened again, if I had an alternative way to waist massive amounts of my time, I would discontinue playing your game.  I have been amazed at the number of times I have had conversations with your staff concerning issues of “verified bugs” just to have an “unverified bug” fixed in the next patch. </P><P>For me, last night was the last straw. I dropped a bag on the ground as I was trying to change out some small backpacks for some larger backpacks.  When this happened I was standing next to wall and I was unable to pick up the backpack.  Heck, I couldn’t even see the backpack. So I logged out and back in hoping to see something change.  I ended up in the wall, as I spun around, just about the time I spot the bag I fall for 10000 points.  That’s bad, what happened next is worse.  I had just completed a raid on Naggy.  I was bound in the Teeth Room and re-spawned there.  While scrolling my chat box to get the 10000 damage message in the screen for a report, I get jumped by a fire giant.  (No I hadn’t re-bound yet, not like I expected to die in Felwith)  Well I hit /quit, just in time and didn’t die again, and again, and again.  I log in with an alt and do a /petition.  Ultimately, I get a response from a representative of yours.  I explain the situation.  I died and I lost a bag.  (There was around 3kpp worth of armor and weapons in the bag BTW).  He says did you do a report? I reply “Yes, Report Kenton.”  While this is all happening I log back into Kenton, and get him back to Felwith.  Your representative decides he can’t help with the bag, “But I lost it due to a bug in Verants program, and I can prove it”.  No reply, nothing.  Ok, “so what happening next” Your representative was not on line, I wait assuming he is zoning, 5 minutes, not online, 10 minutes not online, 15 minutes, not online.  </P><P>Well next I am not online.  I am fed up and now I do have an alternative.  I’m canceling my account in favor of playing Anarchy Online.  It’s in Beta, buggy as heck but still more rewarding that EQ is for me now.  </P><P>YOUR GAME IS GREAT; YOUR CUSTOMER SERVICE IS TERRABLE.</P><P><BR>Kenton <BR>Druid <BR>51st Ring of Life<BR>Do Not Meddle in the Affairs of Dragons... For you are Crunchy and Taste Good with Ketchup!!!</font></td>
      </tr>

